WEBVTT

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.616
and it was the first time
that I was told that I had potential

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:33.480
and felt like somebody believed in me.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.376
Nobody ever told me
that I could be a lawyer,

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.056
doctor or engineer.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.496
I mean, how was I supposed to do that?
I couldn't read, write or spell.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.736
I was illiterate.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.320
So I always thought
crime was my way to go.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.176
And then one day

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.456
I was talking to somebody

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:54.080
and he was telling me
about this robbery that we could do.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:55.960
And we did it.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.896
The reality was that I was growing up

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.136
in the strongest
financial nation in the world,